(D8 - the "none" + "move"/"bind" pattern is translated only for string
 literals. LANGUAGE.md:4262-4267: operands "accept string literals, text
 variables, or buffers", and "Vox recognizes this pattern and translates
 it into the correct MS_MOVE/MS_BIND mount flags". With
   strace -e trace=mount ./p
 the literal statement reaches mount(2) as
   mount(..., NULL, MS_BIND, NULL) = -1 EPERM
 and the variable statement as
   mount(..., "none", 0, "bind") = -1 EPERM
 Indistinguishable from inside Vox unprivileged (both refused).
 Ran, from the repo root, on the installed vox v0.4.15:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/D8.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the literal pattern was refused
   the variable pattern was refused
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
a text called quay is "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_d8".
Create a directory called quay.
Mount quay at quay with type "none" with options "bind".
On error print "the literal pattern was refused".
a text called 'none word' is "none".
a text called 'bind word' is "bind".
Mount quay at quay with type 'none word' with options 'bind word'.
On error print "the variable pattern was refused".
Remove the directory called quay.
